----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = x + 1
end fun

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

call bump(mut b)

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let c = b * 2

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 3 | reads `bump` (2), updates `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 252 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

fun bump(mut x: int)
  set x = x * 2
end fun

----------
expect the function's body is edited
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 reruns and updates `b`, so `b` has to be as unit 3 first found it | `b` = 250 |
| 2 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | - |
| 3 | reads `bump` (2), updates `b` (1) | reruns | reads `bump` | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3 | `c` = 500 |

----------
scriptunit-insert 5 after 1
----------

fun lower(mut x: int)
  set x = x - 25
end fun
call lower(mut b)

----------
expect a unit that defines a function and calls it on `b` is inserted after unit 1
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 5 updates `b`, which unit 3 updated since | `b` = 200 |
| 5 | updates `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |
| 2 | - | untouched | nothing changed `bump` | - |
| 3 | reads `bump` (2), updates `b` (1) | reruns | updates `b` after unit 5 | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 5 | `c` = 400 |

