scriptunit-delete 5
----------

----------
expect unit 5 is deleted
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 5 updated `b` when it last ran, and is deleted | `b` = 250 |
| 5 | - | deleted | deleted | - |
| 2 | - | untouched | nothing changed `bump` | - |
| 3 | reads `bump` (2), updates `b` (1) | reruns | updates `b`, which unit 5 no longer updates first | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3 | `c` = 500 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

fun bump(ref x: int): int
  ret x + 1
end fun

----------
expect the function stops writing its argument
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 updated `b` when it last ran, and no longer compiles | `b` = 125 |
| 2 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | - |
| 3 | - | recompile fails | `bump` no longer takes `mut` | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b`, which unit 3 no longer updates | `c` = 250 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 3
----------

set b = bump(ref b)

----------
expect the call is edited to suit
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | `b` is as unit 1 made it | `b` = 126 |
| 2 | - | untouched | nothing changed `bump` | - |
| 3 | reads `bump` (2), updates `b` (1) | recompiles, runs | edited | - |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3, which now updates it | `c` = 252 |
